e Image; codec tests do not need Docker or extra dependencies.\",\nstats/io.netty/netty-codec/4.2.1.Final/execution-metrics.json:84:      \"agent_guidance\": \"Set system property io.netty.allocator.type=unpooled before any Netty class initializes, for both JVM and native-test execution. Netty documents adaptive as the 4.2 default and supports selecting unpooled via this property: https://netty.io/wiki/analyzing-memory-allocator-behavior.html\",\nstats/io.netty/netty-common/5.0.0.Alpha1/execution-metrics.json:100:      \"agent_guidance\": \"No required environment or system-property setup. Keep generated tests scoped to netty-common APIs such as Version, AttributeKey/DefaultAttributeMap, ResourceLeakDetector, Recycler, ReferenceCounted, timers, promises/executors, and internal utility paths only when they compile on Netty 5. Avoid reusing old tests that import netty-codec-http, netty-transport, or Netty 4 handler APIs.\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
